Review for concurrency defects only. The worker count and queue size are accepted policy.

```go
type Pool struct { cancel context.CancelFunc; wg sync.WaitGroup; jobs chan Job }
func (p *Pool) worker(ctx context.Context) {
    defer p.wg.Done()
    for {
        select {
        case <-ctx.Done(): return
        case job, ok := <-p.jobs:
            if !ok { return }
            process(ctx, job)
        }
    }
}
func (p *Pool) Close() { p.cancel(); p.wg.Wait() }
```
All workers are added before launch, only the producer closes jobs, sends select on ctx.Done, and Close is guarded by sync.Once in the omitted constructor-owned code.
